-- title:
--   Minimal primes over t in the chart W[x,y]/(xy-t)
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and $t \in W$, and assume that the quotient ring $W/(t)$ is an integral domain (in particular nonzero, so $t$ is not a unit). Write $C =$ `CrossingQuotient W t` for the quotient of the polynomial ring $W[X_0,X_1]$ in two variables over $W$ by the principal ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - t$, and let `U t`, `V t` denote the two distinguished elements of $C$ attached to this presentation. The assertion is twofold. First, the set of minimal primes of the ideal of $C$ generated by the image of $t$ under the structure map $W \to C$ — that is, the set of prime ideals of $C$ containing $t$ that are minimal with this property — is exactly the two-element set consisting of the principal ideals generated by `U t` and by `V t`. Second, those two principal ideals are distinct. Thus the special fibre over $t$ of this chart has exactly two irreducible components, cut out by `U t` and by `V t` respectively.
--
--   This is the local computation identifying the two branches of the fibre $\operatorname{Spec} (W/(t))[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1)$ of a crossing chart $W[x,y]/(xy-t)$, the polynomial analogue of the standard description of $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$. It is used in the analysis of the resolution built from such charts, in [`MvPolynomial.CrossingQuotient.Resolution.eq_iota_apply_of_specializes_of_notMem_preimage_basicOpen`](thm.html#MvPolynomial.CrossingQuotient.Resolution.eq_iota_apply_of_specializes_of_notMem_preimage_basicOpen).
